			JEST FOR KIDS 11-09-10
		Riddles and Puns for the 8 to 14 year old

			RIDDLES

What do an elephant and a tree have in common?
    Both have trunks

What is the first trick zombies teach their dogs?
    To play dead.

How does a dog stop a VCR?
    He presses the paws button.

What kind of dinosaur had the best vocabulary?
    A thesauras

What do you get if a tortoise blocks the sun?
    A turtle eclipse.=20

What kind of case would a lawyer bring if he hurt himself while swimming =
in the pool?
    A bathing suit.

			SCHOOL WORK

Define "Acqualntant": A species of tiny insect which you consider to be =
pleasing, odd, or antique.

Use "Ingest" in a sentence: Don=92t take it so seriously. I only meant =
it INGEST.

I came down with laryngitis last week. This was the day our fifth grade =
class was going on a field trip to the zoo and I did not want to miss =
it, so I went to school in spite of having lost my voice. The highlight =
of the visit to the zoo was the time we spent in the petting zoo. While =
I was petting a baby Shetland Pony, my teacher asked, "How are you =
feeling today?." I responded, "I'm feeling a little horse.=94

Excuses: "Dear School: Please ekscuse John being absent on Oct. 28, 29, =
30, 31, 32, and also 33."

"You're a real zero," said Tom naughtily.=20

			PUNS & SHORT JOKES

Headline: 4-H Girls Win Prizes for Fat Calves

I witnessed a robbery in a fabric factory and immediately called the =
police. They caught the culprit and held me as a material witness.

He drove his expensive car into a tree and found out how the Mercedes =
bends.

Show me a man with both feet firmly on the ground, and I'll show you a =
man who can't get his pants off.

Bakers trade bread recipes on a kneed to know basis.

I took a part time job as an opinion poll sampler. On my very first =
call, I introduced myself, "Hello, this is a telephone poll."

			GROANERS & LONG JOKES

A fellow took his girlfriend, Bitzi, a natural blonde, to the movies. =
During the previews, she asked him if he would go and buy her some M&Ms. =
When he returned with her candy, she opened the bag, picked out all the =
brown ones and threw them away. "What did you do that for?" he asked =
her. "I'm allergic to chocolate!" she replied.

Our neighbor came home with a birdhouse one day. I kidded him, asking =
how many birds cold afford to live in our  neighborhood. "Leave that to =
me," he replied. Soon that birdhouse was dangling from a tree with a =
sign that read: "Room for wren -- cheep."=20


